1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,051
Hello everyone.

2
00:00:01,051 --> 00:00:03,643
Today, I will be presenting LaGarNet:

3
00:00:03,643 --> 00:00:09,388
a latent world model designed for quasi-static,
pick-and-place garment flattening.

4
00:00:09,388 --> 00:00:15,133
We show that a single policy trained
entirely in simulation flattens four distinct

5
00:00:15,133 --> 00:00:17,305
garment types on real hardware,

6
00:00:17,305 --> 00:00:19,267
with no further fine-tuning.

7
00:00:19,617 --> 00:00:22,381
Our primary task is garment flattening,

8
00:00:22,381 --> 00:00:28,124
a critical prerequisite for downstream
tasks like folding, ironing, and pressing.

9
00:00:28,124 --> 00:00:34,079
This task is inherently challenging because
cloth possesses vast degrees of freedom,

10
00:00:34,079 --> 00:00:36,986
undergoes severe non-linear deformations,

11
00:00:36,986 --> 00:00:41,310
and exhibits high self-occlusion
from a top-down perspective.

12
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:47,265
To rigorously evaluate the underlying
representation rather than relying on hardware

13
00:00:47,265 --> 00:00:48,045
complexity,

14
00:00:48,045 --> 00:00:52,937
we deliberately constrain our physical
setup to a single robotic arm,

15
00:00:52,937 --> 00:00:57,403
a single pick-and-place primitive,
and one top-down RGB camera.

16
00:00:57,753 --> 00:01:02,322
Existing data-driven flatteners
generally fall into three families.

17
00:01:02,322 --> 00:01:05,732
Behaviour cloning is
conceptually straightforward,

18
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:11,392
but adequately covering the vast state
space of crumpled configurations requires an

19
00:01:11,392 --> 00:01:14,325
impractical volume of
human demonstrations,

20
00:01:14,325 --> 00:01:16,848
often necessitating scripted oracles.

21
00:01:16,848 --> 00:01:21,144
Model-free reinforcement learning
explores this space directly,

22
00:01:21,144 --> 00:01:23,054
yielding general flatteners,

23
00:01:23,054 --> 00:01:28,578
but suffers from poor sample efficiency
and cannot predict the forward effects of

24
00:01:28,578 --> 00:01:29,123
actions.

25
00:01:29,123 --> 00:01:32,942
Model-based methods remain
rare in garment manipulation;

26
00:01:32,942 --> 00:01:38,125
standard latent models tend to produce
blurred reconstructions that lose the

27
00:01:38,125 --> 00:01:41,944
critical edge and corner
features necessary for shaping.

28
00:01:41,944 --> 00:01:44,740
This leads to our core research question:

29
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:50,400
can latent world models built for continuous
control still function in quasi-static

30
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,560
primitive setups,

31
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:55,720
where consecutive observations
are not temporally continuous?

32
00:01:56,070 --> 00:02:01,852
Our solution is LaGarNet, built upon a
goal-conditioned recurrent state-space model.

33
00:02:01,852 --> 00:02:07,429
The fundamental design choice here is the
direct integration of goal-conditioning

34
00:02:07,429 --> 00:02:10,251
into the latent inference process itself.

35
00:02:10,251 --> 00:02:15,690
Both the prior and posterior distributions
over the latent state are explicitly

36
00:02:15,690 --> 00:02:16,447
goal-aware.

37
00:02:16,447 --> 00:02:21,817
A recurrent backbone maintains a belief
state over the occluded regions of the

38
00:02:21,817 --> 00:02:22,368
garment,

39
00:02:22,368 --> 00:02:27,462
while a joint decoder predicts both
the top-down mask and the task reward.

40
00:02:27,462 --> 00:02:31,387
During inference, we plan
using the cross-entropy method,

41
00:02:31,387 --> 00:02:36,963
sampling candidate pick-and-place actions
and ranking them based on the predicted

42
00:02:36,963 --> 00:02:37,445
reward.

43
00:02:37,445 --> 00:02:43,021
Ablation studies reveal that removing
goal-conditioning from the latent inference

44
00:02:43,021 --> 00:02:47,290
costs twenty-two and a half
percentage points of success rate,

45
00:02:47,290 --> 00:02:51,076
from seventy-five percent
down to fifty-two and a half.

46
00:02:51,426 --> 00:02:55,148
Our second contribution is
the data collection paradigm.

47
00:02:55,148 --> 00:02:59,802
We train a Diffusion Policy expert
on just fifty human demonstrations,

48
00:02:59,802 --> 00:03:05,385
allowing it to reliably reach near-flattened
states that a random exploration policy

49
00:03:05,385 --> 00:03:06,848
would rarely discover.

50
00:03:06,848 --> 00:03:12,298
We then mix this expert's rollouts in a
one-to-one ratio with a mask-biased random

51
00:03:12,298 --> 00:03:12,764
policy,

52
00:03:12,764 --> 00:03:18,148
which drives state exploration by uniformly
sampling pick points exclusively from

53
00:03:18,148 --> 00:03:20,275
the garment's segmentation mask.

54
00:03:20,275 --> 00:03:25,726
This approach yields a robust dataset of
five thousand episodes without relying on

55
00:03:25,726 --> 00:03:27,388
complex scripted oracles,

56
00:03:27,388 --> 00:03:32,838
creating a paradigm that is agnostic to
cloth dynamics and likely to generalise to

57
00:03:32,838 --> 00:03:34,833
other deformable object tasks.

58
00:03:35,183 --> 00:03:39,588
Our third contribution is a
novel coverage-alignment reward.

59
00:03:39,588 --> 00:03:43,920
This metric jointly evaluates
state coverage and alignment,

60
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:48,178
computed entirely from top-down
binary segmentation masks.

61
00:03:48,178 --> 00:03:48,912
Crucially,

62
00:03:48,912 --> 00:03:54,786
it eliminates the need for privileged
particle-level state or learned smoothness

63
00:03:54,786 --> 00:03:55,594
estimators.

64
00:03:55,594 --> 00:04:01,594
This allows the exact same continuous and
linear reward function to be evaluated in

65
00:04:01,687 --> 00:04:04,991
simulation and directly
on physical hardware,

66
00:04:04,991 --> 00:04:08,589
making it highly amenable
to predictive learning.

67
00:04:08,939 --> 00:04:12,312
In simulation, LaGarNet
achieves parity with MEDOR,

68
00:04:12,312 --> 00:04:14,957
the state-of-the-art mesh-based planner,

69
00:04:14,957 --> 00:04:20,247
whilst outperforming both PlaNet-ClothPick
and Diffusion Policy across short and

70
00:04:20,247 --> 00:04:21,901
medium planning horizons.

71
00:04:21,901 --> 00:04:23,356
Furthermore, a single,

72
00:04:23,356 --> 00:04:27,786
unified policy trained across all
garments outperforms specialised,

73
00:04:27,786 --> 00:04:29,373
single-garment variants,

74
00:04:29,373 --> 00:04:34,201
suggesting that morphological diversity
acts as a beneficial regulariser.

75
00:04:34,201 --> 00:04:34,928
Ultimately,

76
00:04:34,928 --> 00:04:40,483
the policy exceeds ninety-five percent
normalised coverage across all four simulated

77
00:04:40,483 --> 00:04:43,526
garment categories within
twenty action steps.

78
00:04:43,876 --> 00:04:47,899
This comparison also has a
crucial computational dimension.

79
00:04:47,899 --> 00:04:53,491
LaGarNet requires five times fewer parameters
than MEDOR and plans seventeen times

80
00:04:53,491 --> 00:04:53,969
faster,

81
00:04:53,969 --> 00:04:56,356
with no loss in flattening quality.

82
00:04:56,356 --> 00:05:01,061
Six seconds of planning per action
is affordable on a physical robot,

83
00:05:01,061 --> 00:05:03,994
where one hundred and
three seconds is not.

84
00:05:03,994 --> 00:05:09,654
We are careful not to overstate this: with
perception and robot execution included,

85
00:05:09,654 --> 00:05:14,428
a single real manipulation step still
takes about twenty-four seconds,

86
00:05:14,428 --> 00:05:19,202
so the full perception-action cycle
remains the deployment bottleneck.

87
00:05:19,552 --> 00:05:25,232
We subsequently transferred this
simulation-trained policy directly to a physical

88
00:05:25,232 --> 00:05:26,424
UR5e robotic arm,

89
00:05:26,424 --> 00:05:29,790
achieving this with zero
real-world fine-tuning.

90
00:05:29,790 --> 00:05:34,628
The videos shown here demonstrate
rollouts on all four garment types,

91
00:05:34,628 --> 00:05:37,152
accelerated to ten times real speed.

92
00:05:37,152 --> 00:05:42,201
The policy operates solely on a
top-down observation and the goal image,

93
00:05:42,201 --> 00:05:47,600
and the reward is computed from the
exact same segmentation masks utilised in

94
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:48,372
simulation.

95
00:05:48,372 --> 00:05:53,981
This consistency is precisely what enables
successful zero-shot transfer without

96
00:05:53,981 --> 00:05:58,118
requiring a highly tuned digital
twin of the physical cell.

97
00:05:58,469 --> 00:06:03,883
Quantitatively, across forty physical
trials of twenty actions each,

98
00:06:03,883 --> 00:06:09,058
LaGarNet achieves ninety point
three percent normalised coverage,

99
00:06:09,058 --> 00:06:13,039
eighty point seven percent
normalised improvement,

100
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:18,453
and an eighty-one point one percent
maximum intersection over union.

101
00:06:18,453 --> 00:06:23,150
It successfully completes
twenty-seven out of forty trials,

102
00:06:23,150 --> 00:06:27,927
against nine out of forty for
the PlaNet-ClothPick baseline,

103
00:06:27,927 --> 00:06:33,023
though a human operator still
reaches thirty-eight out of forty.

104
00:06:33,023 --> 00:06:39,023
Success here means reaching eighty-five
percent coverage and seventy-five percent

105
00:06:39,472 --> 00:06:45,363
maximum intersection over union at any
point within a twenty-step episode;

106
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:51,363
we relax these thresholds from their
simulation values to allow for the sim-to-real

107
00:06:51,972 --> 00:06:52,290
gap.

108
00:06:52,290 --> 00:06:55,316
We also stress-tested a fifth garment,

109
00:06:55,316 --> 00:07:01,316
a soft long-sleeved dress whose topology
is absent from the simulated training set.

110
00:07:01,924 --> 00:07:07,924
Evaluated separately over ten further
trials, the policy recovers most of its area,

111
00:07:08,532 --> 00:07:14,344
at seventy-seven percent coverage,
but never meets the success criterion,

112
00:07:14,344 --> 00:07:16,255
scoring zero out of ten.

113
00:07:16,605 --> 00:07:19,619
We draw two primary
lessons from this work.

114
00:07:19,619 --> 00:07:20,040
First,

115
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:25,718
latent world models can be highly effective
in quasi-static manipulation regimes,

116
00:07:25,718 --> 00:07:31,326
provided that goal-conditioning is
integrated directly into the latent inference

117
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:31,886
process.

118
00:07:31,886 --> 00:07:36,443
Second, greedy, one-step planning
yields the highest performance.

119
00:07:36,443 --> 00:07:41,630
Because a single manipulation primitive
induces massive state deformation,

120
00:07:41,630 --> 00:07:47,448
predictive error compounds faster than
extended lookahead can provide value—success

121
00:07:47,448 --> 00:07:51,654
drops from seventy-three point
three percent at horizon one,

122
00:07:51,654 --> 00:07:54,037
to thirty percent at horizon five.

123
00:07:54,037 --> 00:07:59,785
The principal limitation of our current
system is the lack of an explicit stopping

124
00:07:59,785 --> 00:08:00,486
criterion.

125
00:08:00,486 --> 00:08:05,954
Immediate future work includes integrating
a learned termination condition and

126
00:08:05,954 --> 00:08:09,389
extending the framework
to goal-directed folding.

127
00:08:09,389 --> 00:08:10,370
Looking ahead,

128
00:08:10,370 --> 00:08:15,978
we view this formulation as a promising
pathway toward general deformable-object

129
00:08:15,978 --> 00:08:16,889
manipulation.

130
00:08:16,889 --> 00:08:18,572
Thank you for listening.
